Xsession: keep the X server from resetting before dtsession connects

Started by a display manager other than dtlogin (lightdm, sddm, ...),
Xsession may be the only thing talking to the X server. Each short
lived client it runs (xset fp+, ...) is then the last one to close,
the server resets, and the CDE font aliases are dropped from the font
path before dthello and dtsession start: Motif falls back to fixed
fonts. Hold one connection open until dtsession is up.

--- a/programs/dtlogin/config/_common.ksh.src	2026-11-08 23:25:25.826978867 -0300
+++ b/programs/dtlogin/config/_common.ksh.src	2026-11-08 23:25:25.839979756 -0300
@@ -42,6 +42,32 @@
   pexec=$(LC_TIME=C /usr/bin/ps -p $PPID | awk 'NR==2 {print $4}')
 #endif
   Log "Xsession started by $pexec"
+
+  HASH
+  HASH Keep a connection to the X server open until dtsession is up.
+  HASH Display managers other than dtlogin may leave no client connected
+  HASH while this script runs, and every short lived client below (xset,
+  HASH xrdb, ...) then makes the server reset when it exits, which drops
+  HASH the font path set here. The keeper is released once dtsession has
+  HASH published _DT_SM_WINDOW_INFO on the root window, or after 120s.
+  HASH
+  if [ "${pexec##*/}" != "dtlogin" ] && [ -x $XDIR/xprop ]; then
+    $XDIR/xprop -root -spy _DT_SM_WINDOW_INFO 2>&1 |&
+    dtstart_keepalive=$!
+    read -p REPLY
+    exec 3<&p
+    exec 3<&-
+    $XDIR/xprop -root -remove _DT_SM_WINDOW_INFO >/dev/null 2>&1
+    (
+      i=0
+      while [ $i -lt 120 ]; do
+        sleep 1
+        $XDIR/xprop -root _DT_SM_WINDOW_INFO 2>/dev/null | grep -q " = " && break
+        i=$((i + 1))
+      done
+      kill $dtstart_keepalive
+    ) >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+  fi
 #endif
 
 XCOMM ##########################################################################
